<title>CANADA: Canada flax oil content seen 44.2 pct, above avg.</title>
<headline>Canada flax oil content seen 44.2 pct, above avg.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's 1996 flaxseed oil content was forecast at 44.2 percent, slightly above last year's content of 44.1 percent and above the 1986/95 average of 43.8 percent, the Canadian Grain Commission said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;This preliminary estimate is based on about 50 percent of the total samples normally received. If no significant changes occur in later samples, the overall 1996 Canadian flaxseed crop should be near average in oil content and oil quality (iodine value) and only slightly lower than last year in protein content,&quot; the CGC said.</p>
<p>Test results were based on 255 samples on November 28.  </p>
